id: pm-tqel
title: "Consolidate history commands: history-redact/history-repair/history-compact/activity/restore under pm history subcommands"
description: "pm history <id> stays the default view; history-redact -> pm history redact, history-repair -> pm history repair, history-compact -> pm history compact, activity -> pm history activity, restore -> pm history restore (old spellings aliased). Duplicate check: no existing history-namespace item; history feature items are all closed deliverables."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:history",simplification
created_at: "2026-07-05T04:53:05.215Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-07T22:43:18.682Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-07T22:33:28.184Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-07T22:33:28.184Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: pm history gains redact/repair/compact/activity/restore subcommands with flag parity; old top-level spellings alias-shimmed with identical output; default pm history <id> view unchanged; contracts/MCP/completions/docs regenerated; existing history-* specs pass via aliases
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Expose native history redact, repair, compact, activity and restore through shared SDK contracts and permanent aliases. Preserve native/legacy addressing, output, recovery and privacy. Restrict inherited redaction recovery rewrites to the leading command path; reject bulk-only min-entries in single-ID compaction; explicitly retain diagnostic maintenance report envelopes alongside the restore mutation receipt. Resolve shell operation completion after recognized global prefixes and values, preserving ordinary history arguments and native/legacy parity across Bash, Zsh and Fish. Scope matcher-value redaction to the leading native or legacy command path after bootstrap globals, preserving unrelated diagnostic values. Resolve native history transcript output and exit contracts through the selected canonical operation, and expose value-taking item-ID completion in Zsh and Fish. Exercise native recovery strings directly in the existing native/legacy privacy fixture."
expected_result: "Native and compatibility history operations preserve output, exit, privacy, transcript and completion contracts across globals and positional boundaries."
actual_result: "All 8555 tests across 639 files pass at exact 100% coverage in all four metrics; three linked suites and focused ESLint pass. Native recovery fixture strings now follow the tested command form. Source is unchanged from 94532b596, whose full hosted static chain, all five Nightly jobs and exact-head analyzers passed. The test/tracker commit still requires fresh full review and hosted validation."
