  "2026-09-07T21:56:08.781Z","harness:codex","All 8555 tests passed with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and zero uncovered counts after sequential execution with fixtures in /var/tmp. The local static chain reached the unchanged startup timing gate, then failed five operations (get/context/next/create/claim). An unchanged prior build on the same host failed the same five bounds (404/448/475/429/427 ms versus 362/433/440/398/415 ms). Comparing the installed prior candidate with this build found 595 unchanged JS files; the CLI entry code is identical after normalizing generated chunk references. This is recorded as a local timing limitation, not a passing gate. The unchanged complete pnpm quality:static command in the Linux Node 24 Nightly job remains mandatory before merge. Remaining graph/record checks are being completed separately; no threshold or gate is weakened."
  "2026-09-07T21:56:19.865Z","harness:codex","History transcript and item-ID completion corrections verified: all 8555 tests across 639 files passed with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and zero uncovered counts. Source, documentation, import-cost, security and static assurance gates passed. The local cold-start timing gate exceeded unchanged limits; an unchanged prior build failed the same five operations on the same host. The compiled CLI entry is identical after generated chunk-name normalization. Graph and record-integrity checks passed separately. The complete unchanged static chain must pass in hosted Nightly before merge; local timing failure is not being called a pass. All three linked suites, focused ESLint and documentation links passed. Both new regressions failed before correction; all 28 focused tests then passed. Transcript validation uses dependency-light root/operation scanning and canonical history aliases for both output and exit contracts, preserves argv, rejects contradictory output families and retains ordinary history IDs, globals and delimiters. The output-envelope resolver itself was already correct. Zsh/Fish expose value-taking --id for redact, repair and compact; real Bash, Zsh and Fish each passed 59 native/legacy/global-prefix cases. Fresh npm/Bun installations verified all history journeys, public SDK transcript parity and refusal, and ID completion. Packed npx/bunx/TypeScript smoke passed. Coverage was restarted sequentially after overlapping build preparation touched dist, then moved to /var/tmp after fixture writes exhausted /tmp; no tests or gates were weakened. Regular prior-head PR checks passed; the new head still requires fresh full review and all hosted/platform verification before merge. No same-day republication is claimed."
