  "2026-09-07T22:25:37.830Z","harness:codex","The existing native/legacy recovery fixture now derives attempted_command and suggested_retry from the tested command array while preserving argv and literal matcher values. All three focused tests, all three linked suites and focused ESLint passed. SDK/CLI source is byte-for-byte unchanged from 94532b596, whose full hosted static chain and five platform jobs passed. This is a fixture correction, not a newly reproduced source bug; full exact coverage is running on the strengthened fixture. All six current bot artifacts were read and acknowledged, including the edited completion-fix confirmation."
  "2026-09-07T22:33:27.630Z","harness:codex","Native recovery fixture correction verified: all 8555 tests across 639 files pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage with zero uncovered counts. All three focused tests, all three linked suites and focused ESLint pass. attempted_command and suggested_retry now use the tested command array, retaining literal matcher values and argv; source code is unchanged from 94532b596. This is fixture strengthening, not a new source bug. The unchanged source passed all regular PR checks, all five Nightly jobs including full static quality and compatibility (34165269157), and exact-head zero-issue CodeFactor/DeepScan. Required Sentry/telemetry reliability also passed. Full base-to-head review found only this fixture gap; every current review artifact was read and acknowledged. The next commit still requires fresh full review and hosted checks before merge. GitHub intake separately records open unclaimed package-copy planning in pm-5bsofk (#1218) and the reproduced claim receipt gap in canonical pm-nilh (#437); neither is claimed as implemented by this history delivery."
